{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"24497","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/24497","key":"MC-279570","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"16/Jan/25 6:10 AM","customfield_10050":"1357236","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>After the fix of \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-279326\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-279326\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Lit observers no longer send block updates when moved by a piston\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-279326\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n, some piston operations still don't cause neighbor updates, as they used to before 25w02a. This means many redstone contraptions containing piston blocks may break.</p>\n\n<p>Steps to reproduce:<br>\nFollow the visual instructions in the attached video.<br>\nThe redstone dust is supposed to depower after the lever is destroyed by the piston.</p>\n\n<p>Code analysis and proposed solution:<br>\nThis issue still persists because the observer subissue(\n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"MC-279326\">\n                <a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-279326\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\" title=\"Lit observers no longer send block updates when moved by a piston\">\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\">\n            MC-279326\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Resolved</span>\n            </span>\n) seems to have been fixed by allowing the <tt>UPDATE_MOVE_BY_PISTON</tt> flag, in alternative to <tt>UPDATE_NEIGHBORS</tt>, to also cause calling <tt>BlockStateBase#affectNeighborsAfterRemoval</tt>, but two of the different combinations of flags in <tt>PistonBaseBlock#moveBlocks</tt> don't contain the <tt>UPDATE_MOVE_BY_PISTON</tt> flag, thus causing the general issue of missing updates to partly persist.<br>\nI would encourage fixing this by removing the <tt>UPDATE_MOVE_BY_PISTON</tt> flag check in <tt>LevelChunk#setBlockState</tt> and instead adding the <tt>UPDATE_NEIGHBORS</tt> flag (either in-place or an intermediate method) to any place <tt>UPDATE_MOVE_BY_PISTON</tt> is used and a neighbor update is expected, and to all the combinations of flags in <tt>PistonBaseBlock#moveBlocks</tt>, except the <tt>UPDATE_NONE | UPDATE_KNOWN_SHAPE</tt> combination (that one would actually negatively impact the current behavior if modified because sticky pistons pulling a block are not supposed to cause a neighbor update on retraction).</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"16/Jan/25 2:12 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/42571","id":"42571","filename":"missing_neighbor_updates_on_piston_breaking_lever.mp4","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"VelizarBG","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Helsinki","accountType":"customer"},"created":"16/Jan/25 10:09 AM","size":"3.79 MB","mimeType":"video/mp4","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/42571"}],"versions":null,"resolutiondate":"22/Jan/25 3:00 AM","issuelinks":null,"updated":"10/Aug/26 2:48 AM","status":null},"fields":{"summary":"Some piston operations don't send neighbor updates","issuetype":{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issuetype/10006","id":"10006","description":"A problem which impairs or prevents the functions of the product. (Migrated on 23 Jan 2025 19:08 UTC)","iconUrl":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium","name":"Bug","subtask":false,"avatarId":10303,"hierarchyLevel":0},"watches":{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/MC-279570/watchers","watchCount":1,"isWatching":false},"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":null,"created":"2025-01-16T06:10:51.661-0800","customfield_10050":"1357236","customfield_10051":{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/customFieldOption/10095","value":"Expansion A","id":"10095"},"description":{"type":"doc","version":1,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"After the fix of "},{"type":"inlineCard","attrs":{"url":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/browse/MC-279326#icft=MC-279326"}},{"type":"text","text":", some piston operations still don't cause neighbor updates, as they used to before 25w02a. This means many redstone contraptions containing piston blocks may break."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steps to reproduce:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Follow the visual instructions in the attached video."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"The redstone dust is supposed to depower after the lever is destroyed by the piston."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text"